  {
   "thing": {
    "kind": "text",
    "text": "BOUNCING\n\n[my thing, a step, the edge]\n\nThe edge is a READING: one\npad saying which edge the\nstar is against, or \"none\".\n\nThree robots, in order,\ndiffering only in the word\nthey expect:\n\n  left    flip, then move\n  right   flip, then move\n  any     move"
   },
   "x": -1.45,
   "z": 2.15
  },
  {
   "thing": {
    "kind": "text",
    "text": "TO RUN IT\n\nSet Speed to 8x and give the\nwork box to the team leader.\nIt runs until you take the\nbox back or press Pause.\n\nThe star runs to the right\nedge, turns round, runs back,\nturns again, and keeps going.\n\nWatch the team take turns:\nthe two turners look and step\naside all the way across, and\ntake the floor at the edge."
   },
   "x": -0.75,
   "z": 2.15
  },
  {
   "thing": {
    "kind": "text",
    "text": "WHY A READING\n\nAn event would leave the nest\nempty most of the time -- and\na team member facing a bare\nnest dozes, which stops the\nwhole team, including the one\ndoing the moving.\n\nA reading is never empty, so\nevery member can be decided\nevery round.\n\nFlipping the step is a x-1\ndropped on a number. Nothing\nhere is about bouncing."
   },
   "x": -0.05,
   "z": 2.15
  }
